# Local development overrides. Copy to .dev.vars (git-ignored) and uncomment what you need.
#
# The tarot site deploys and serves readings with none of this set, which is why the
# Deploy to Cloudflare button asks you for nothing. ADMIN_PASSWORD is the one you
# have to set anyway, because the operator console does not open without it.

# Relaxes the https-only / no-private-IP checks so you can point at a local agent.
# ENVIRONMENT=development

# Manyfold API base. Defaults to the value in wrangler.jsonc; use staging for local dev.
# MANYFOLD_API_BASE_URL=https://api-staging.manyfold.ai

# The password for the operator console. Every API route except /api/health,
# /api/state and /api/tarot/* requires it as an `x-admin-password` header.
#
# Leaving this unset does NOT open the console — it closes it against everyone,
# yourself included. There is no default password: this repository is public, and a
# lock committed to a public repo is one only its author holds the key to. So the
# console starts shut and says which secret to set (src/worker/admin.ts).
#
# A secret can be as short as you like — nobody, including you afterwards, can read
# it back out of Cloudflare.
#   npx wrangler secret put ADMIN_PASSWORD
# ADMIN_PASSWORD=

# Encrypts the Manyfold device code and agent tokens stored in D1.
# If unset, a random key is generated on first use and stored in the same database.
# Set this (>=32 chars) to keep the key out of the database:
#   npx wrangler secret put CONFIG_ENCRYPTION_KEY
# CONFIG_ENCRYPTION_KEY=
